SUMMARY:🍂 Fall Walk of Toronto Island 🌊🌆! 9KM
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🍂
 🌊 FALL WALK: TORONTO ISLANDS 🌊🍁\n\n### Island Paths\, Fall Colour
 s & Toronto's Best Urban Escape\n\nThere is something magical about the To
 ronto Islands in the fall.\nOnce the summer crowds disappear\, the islands
  become quieter and more peaceful. The changing leaves\, crisp air\, open 
 green spaces\, quiet cottages\, and golden light over the water make it on
 e of the best times of year to explore.\nAnd then there's the skyline.\n\n
 From the islands\, you get some of the best views of Toronto anywhere in t
 he city — especially when the fall colours frame the downtown skyline ac
 ross the water.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed fall walk through **Hanlan's Poin
 t\, Centre Island\, and Ward's Island**\, enjoying the scenery\, fresh air
 \, and great conversation along the way.\nThis is approximately **9 km**\,
  with mostly flat paths and no major hills. It's a longer walk\, but the p
 ace will be relaxed and we'll take breaks along the way\n\n📱 Don't forg
 et to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com
 /H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'
 ll take the **10:15 AM Ward's Island Ferry** and begin our walk once we ar
 rive.\n\nOur route will take us through:\n🌿 Hanlan's Point\n🍂 Centre
  Island\n🏡 Ward's Island\n📸 Skyline viewpoints\n🌊 Waterfront path
 ways\n🍁 Fall foliage and quiet island roads\n\nWe'll stop along the way
  to enjoy the scenery\, take photos\, have a snack\, and spend some time g
 etting to know each other.\n\nAlthough we'll pass several beaches\, **we w
 on't be stopping at them during this event**. We have a route to follow an
 d a ferry to catch!\n\nOur return ferry will be the **2:45 PM Ward's Islan
 d Ferry** back to downtown Toronto.\n\nExpect approximately **3½ to 4 hou
 rs**\, including the ferry rides and breaks.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weathe
 r & Expectations\n\nThe islands can feel quite different from downtown Tor
 onto\, especially in the fall. Expect cooler temperatures\, wind off the l
 ake\, and changing weather.\nPlease dress in layers and bring a jacket or 
 sweater.\nThis is a **social walk\, not a guided historical tour**. I'll s
 hare interesting facts along the way\, but the focus is enjoying the islan
 ds together.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:**
  **INSIDE the Jack Layton Ferry Terminal after your ticket has been scanne
 d.**\nWe are meeting **inside the paid waiting area beside the washrooms.*
 *\n**Please do NOT wait outside the terminal.**\n\nOnce your ferry ticket 
 has been scanned\, walk into the waiting area and you'll find me wearing m
 y **Moose Hat**. 🫎\n\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **10:00 AM**\n🚢 **Ward's 
 Island Ferry LEAVES AT:** **10:15 AM**\n\nPlease be on time. **Once the fe
 rry leaves\, it will be extremely difficult to catch up with the group.**\
 n🚢 **Return Ferry:** 2:45 PM from Ward's Island\n🎟️ **Ferry Ticket
 :** $9.19\n\nYou must purchase your ferry ticket **before signing up for t
 he event.**\n[CLICK HERE FOR FERRY TICKETS](https://secure.toronto.ca/Ferr
 yTicketOnline/tickets2/index.jsp)\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 
 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis f
 ee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events thr
 oughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfo
 rtable walking shoes\n🥨 A snack\n🧥 A warm fall jacket or sweater\n
 🕶️ Sunglasses\n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who 
 Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* Anyone who loves fall 🍂\n*
  People who enjoy exploring Toronto's parks\n* Anyone looking for a longer
  but easy walk\n* People who enjoy beautiful scenery and photography\n* An
 yone who wants to meet new people\n* People who want to escape the city wi
 thout actually leaving it\n\nThe activity is the container. **The people y
 ou meet along the way are the real experience.**\n\n***\n\n**Come for the 
 island paths.**\n**Stay for the fall colours.**\n**Leave feeling like you 
 spent the day on vacation — without ever leaving Toronto.** 🍂🌊\n\n
 You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're 
 unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes plans change and events may need to
  be cancelled\, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n
 👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\
 n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**
