SUMMARY: 🌿 FALL WALK -  Walk: Tommy Thompson Park (Come See The Skyline
 ) 🐦 - 12KM
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🍂
 🐦 Fall Walk: Tommy Thompson Park 🌊\n\n### Wildlife\, Lake Views & On
 e of Toronto's Best Fall Walks\n\nLooking for a walk that feels like you'v
 e left the city without actually leaving Toronto?\n\nJoin us for a fall wa
 lk through **Tommy Thompson Park**\, one of Toronto's most unique outdoor 
 spaces.\nThe park is famous for its wildlife and birding\, with **more tha
 n 300 species recorded**\, as well as its beautiful views across Lake Onta
 rio and back toward the Toronto skyline.\nIn the fall\, the cooler air and
  quieter trails make this a particularly nice time to explore the park. We
 'll follow the trails toward the **lighthouse**\, take a break along the w
 ay\, and then make our way back.\n\nIt's a **long walk**\, but the terrain
  is generally easy. The goal is to enjoy the scenery\, get some fresh air\
 , and spend a few hours walking and talking with other people.\n\n📱 Don
 't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whats
 app.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do
 \n\nWe'll meet near the pavilion and begin our walk through Tommy Thompson
  Park.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Explore the park's trails 🌿\n* Look
  for birds and other wildlife 🐦\n* Enjoy views of Lake Ontario 🌊\n* 
 Take in the Toronto skyline 🌆\n* Make our way toward the lighthouse\n* 
 Stop for a break and some photos 📸\n* Loop back to the pavilion\n\nThe 
 walk will take approximately **3 hours\, including a break**.\nThis is a l
 onger walk\, so you should be comfortable walking at a steady pace for sev
 eral hours.\n**No dogs are permitted in the park.**\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall
  Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is an outdoor walk\, and Tommy Thompson ca
 n be exposed to the wind coming off Lake Ontario.\nPlease dress appropriat
 ely for the weather and bring comfortable walking shoes.\n\nThe trail isn'
 t particularly difficult\, but **the distance is the challenge**. If you'r
 e not comfortable being on your feet and walking steadily for around three
  hours\, this may not be the right walk for you.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup 
 Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Near the pavilion and bathrooms\n🫎
  **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI 
 will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n
 🏁 **End Point:** Tommy Thompson Park Pavilion\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meet
 up Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmai
 l.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organi
 zing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🍔 After the Walk\n\nOnce w
 e've finished\, you're welcome to join us for lunch at **Wendy's or Tim Ho
 rtons** nearby.\nIt's completely optional\, but it's a great chance to sit
  down\, refuel\, and continue the conversation after the walk.\n\n***\n\n#
 # 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A
  snack\n🧥 A fall jacket or sweater\n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n\n
 ***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who
  enjoy nature and wildlife 🐦\n* Anyone interested in birdwatching\n* Pe
 ople who love waterfront walks\n* Anyone looking for a longer social walk\
 n* People who want to explore somewhere different in Toronto\n* Anyone who
  enjoys getting outside and meeting new people\n\nThe activity is the cont
 ainer. **The people you meet along the way are the real experience.**\n\nY
 ou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're u
 nsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to
  be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event page for upd
 ates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall o
 r email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the wildlife
 .** 🐦\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n**Leave with a new connection 
 — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛
