SUMMARY:🎬 FREE DOCUMENTARY SCREENING: THE LIBRARIANS + PUB HANGOUT! 
 🍿🍻
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🎬 
 FREE DOCUMENTARY SCREENING: THE LIBRARIANS + PUB HANGOUT! 🍿🍻\n\n**Mo
 nday\\\, October 19\\\, 2026 \\| 6:30 PM screening**\nLooking for somethin
 g meaningful to do on a Monday evening? Join Nick and fellow movie lovers 
 for a **FREE screening of *The Librarians*** at Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
 !\nThis powerful\, timely documentary explores the battle over book bannin
 g and censorship in the United States. It's a thought-provoking film about
  freedom of expression\, access to information\, and the librarians standi
 ng up for the right to read.\nCome for the documentary\, stay for the conv
 ersation!\n\n### 🎥 ABOUT THE MOVIE\n\n**The Librarians (2025)**\nDirect
 ed by Kim A. Snyder\, this acclaimed documentary follows librarians on the
  front lines of an escalating wave of book bans across America.\nAs books 
 addressing race and LGBTQ+ experiences are challenged and removed from sch
 ools and libraries\, librarians find themselves facing harassment\, threat
 s\, and political pressure. The film follows these librarians as they conn
 ect the dots between local controversies and wider efforts to restrict acc
 ess to books and ideas.\nIt's a compelling look at censorship\, democracy\
 , and the people fighting to protect intellectual freedom.\n⏱️ **Runti
 me:** Approximately 92 minutes.\n🎞️ **Watch the official YouTube trai
 ler:**\n[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ykll4MWltsQ](https://www.youtube.
 com/watch?v=Ykll4MWltsQ)\n\n### 📍 WHEN & WHERE\n\n**Monday\, October 19
 \, 2026**\n🕕 **Meet Nick at 6:15 PM**\n📍 Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema\
 , 506 Bloor Street West\, Toronto.\nLook for **Nick and the Meetup sign ou
 tside the cinema doors** so we can connect before the screening.\n🎬 **M
 ovie starts at 6:30 PM.**\n\n### 🎟️ FREE TICKETS — RESERVE YOURS!\n
 \nThis is a FREE event\, but you should reserve your ticket in advance!\n
 👉 **Reserve your free ticket here:**\n[https://boxoffice.hotdocs.ca/web
 sales/pages/info.aspx?evtinfo=662450~cf285ddd-dacb-4f18-89b8-1252c6dcffa6&
 epguid=a2104450-7e47-4369-a17d-c247570c3939&mdy=10%2F19%2F2026&showing=662
 464](https://boxoffice.hotdocs.ca/websales/pages/info.aspx?evtinfo=662450~
 cf285ddd-dacb-4f18-89b8-1252c6dcffa6&epguid=a2104450-7e47-4369-a17d-c24757
 0c3939&mdy=10%2F19%2F2026&showing=662464)\n**PLEASE RESPECT YOUR RSVP!**\n
 Since this is a free screening\, please RSVP only if you genuinely intend 
 to attend. If your plans change\, kindly update your RSVP so others have t
 he opportunity to join us.\n\n### 🍻 AFTER THE MOVIE: [PAUPERS PUB!](htt
 ps://pauperspub.com/)\n\nThe evening doesn't end when the credits roll!\nA
 fter the screening\, we'll head across the street to **[Paupers Pub](https
 ://pauperspub.com/)**[ ](https://pauperspub.com/)to hang out\, grab a drin
 k or something to eat\, and discuss the documentary.\nDid the film change 
 your perspective? What do you think about book bans and censorship? Let's 
 share our thoughts and enjoy some great conversation.\nFood and drinks are
  optional and at your own expense.\n**A free movie\, an interesting docume
 ntary\, and good company. What's not to like?**\nSee you there!\n— Nick 
 🍿
