SUMMARY:👻 Ghost Tour: The Exhibition Grounds 🎡
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 👻 
 Ghost Tour: The Exhibition Grounds 🎡\n\n### Toronto's Haunted Fairgroun
 ds\, Dark History & One Building I Don't Like Being Near\n\nThe Exhibition
  Grounds have spent more than a century hosting crowds\, celebrations\, so
 ldiers\, shows\, and some of Toronto's biggest events.\nBut underneath all
  that history is a darker side.\n\nThe Exhibition Grounds are said to be *
 *one of the most haunted places in Toronto** — and I'll be honest: **thi
 s is the one place on my ghost walks that genuinely scares me.**\n\nThere'
 s something about the atmosphere here.\nSome buildings have an energy that
  feels different. And when you know what happened in them\, it's hard not 
 to look at them a little differently.\n\nOn this evening ghost walk\, we'l
 l explore the grounds and hear stories of **soldiers\, settlers\, performe
 rs\, animals\, tragedies\, and people who may never have completely left.*
 *\n\nThis isn't just about trying to scare you.\nIt's about discovering th
 e strange history hiding underneath one of Toronto's most familiar landmar
 ks.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](htt
 ps://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We
 'll Explore\n\nWe'll begin outside **Medieval Times** and make our way acr
 oss the Exhibition Grounds toward the Princes' Gates.\nAlong the way\, we'
 ll hear stories connected to:\n\n* 🏚️ **The General Service Building*
 *\n* 💀 **The Stanley Barracks** — the building that genuinely creeps 
 me out\n* 🐎 **The Horse Palace**\n* 🏠 **Scadding Cabin**\n* 👻 Oth
 er strange stories\, unexplained encounters\, and haunted corners of the g
 rounds\n\nWe'll finish at the **Princes' Gates**.\nWe'll keep a steady wal
 king pace and **will not be entering any of the buildings**.\n\n***\n\n## 
 🕯️ Why This One Is Different\n\nI've done a lot of ghost walks around
  Toronto.\n**This is the one that actually makes me uncomfortable.**\nMayb
 e it's the history. Maybe it's the buildings. Maybe it's simply knowing wh
 at happened here and then standing there after dark.\n\nWhatever it is\, t
 he Exhibition Grounds have always felt different to me.\n\nSo come prepare
 d for some genuinely creepy stories — and maybe a few moments where we a
 ll wonder whether we should really be standing there. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 
 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** In front of **Medieval Ti
 mes**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 
 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time i
 s late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:*
 * **Princes' Gates**\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in pers
 on or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curate
 d ghost-walking experience**\, rather than one of our regular social walks
 . The route\, stories\, and history have been researched and brought toget
 her specifically for this experience.\nThe fee helps support the time and 
 work that goes into creating these walks.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\
 n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧
  Water\n📱 Your phone for photos\nAnd maybe… don't wander off by yours
 elf. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis experience is great f
 or:\n\n* 👻 People who love ghost stories\n* 🏙️ Anyone fascinated b
 y Toronto's darker history\n* 🕯️ Fans of the strange and unexplained\
 n* 🎡 People who want to see the Exhibition Grounds differently\n* 🚶 
 Anyone looking for something unusual to do on an evening out\n* 😈 Peopl
 e who like being scared — at least a little\n\nYou don't have to believe
  in ghosts.\n**You just have to be willing to walk into the dark with us.*
 *\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just sho
 w up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things ha
 ppen and events may need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an ey
 e on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestion
 s? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmai
 l.com**\n\n**Come for the history.**\n**Stay for the ghost stories.**\n**A
 nd try not to look too closely at the buildings.** 👻
